esponse, a 5xx, 408 or 429. In strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch when one call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in it fails, so the encoder leaves out each call Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything else drops the whole request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it takes that in place of the address it reads from an HTTP request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"code":"pk_...","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are client keys, safe to ship in an app: they let a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client send data to the source and read nothing. Its private keys ("},{"code":"sk_...","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io API, deleting people included, and must not ship in an app, so the factory"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/emptyAPIKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for a key that is empty or only whitespace,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for a private key ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_..."},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"ref